  {
    "knowledge_point": {
      "db_id": 17592186087699,
      "id": "9b9ef325-2358-5041-8a8d-b459e8ed9f09",
      "title": "Determining the Inverse of a 2x2 Matrix"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "08c32bbd-6862-5208-be31-5dda735b62fa",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the matrices\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & \\frac{2}{3} \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & -\\frac{2}{3}\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{2}{3} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2} & -1\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{2}{3} \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & -1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n- **I.** $AB=BA={I}_{2}$\n- **II.** $AC=CA={I}_{2}$\n- **III.** $C={A}^{-1}$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked.",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
      ":question/worked-solution": "- First, we check whether $AB=BA={I}_{2}.$ Computing $AB$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & \\frac{2}{3} \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & -\\frac{2}{3}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{2}{3} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2} & -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\u2217 & \u2217 \\\\ \\frac{2}{3} & \u2217\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \\ne {I}_{2}.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, statement I is false.\n\n- Now, we check whether $AC=CA={I}_{2}.$ Computing $AC$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AC & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & \\frac{2}{3} \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & -\\frac{2}{3}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{2}{3} \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={I}_{2}.\\,\u2713\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLikewise, computing $CA$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}CA & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{2}{3} \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & \\frac{2}{3} \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & -\\frac{2}{3}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={I}_{2}.\\,\u2713\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, statement II is true. As a result, $C={A}^{-1}$ and statement III is true too.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only\".",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "0d7df08b-c854-5c81-ac5b-54b182498667",
          ":answer-field/key": "I",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/checkbox",
